 Steps to Fork (on GitHub)
1. Open any repository.
2. Click Fork (top right).
3. A copy will be created under your account.
Example:
Original repo → github.com/originaluser/project
Forked repo → github.com/yourusername/project
 Clone the Forked Repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/project.git
cd project
 Merge in Git
 What is Merge?
Merging combines changes from one branch into another branch.
 Steps to Merge
Step 1: Create a new branch
git checkout -b feature
Step 2: Make changes and commit
echo "Feature added" >> file.txt
git add .
git commit -m "Added feature"
Step 3: Switch to main branch
git checkout main
Step 4: Merge feature branch
git merge feature
